# check.mustblock -- URLs that MUST NOT be reachable, and check.sh fails while they are.
#
# One URL per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. EVERY LINE NEEDS A REASON.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS, and it is the inverse of everything else check.sh does. On 2026-09-15 that scan
# found `/engcalcs/.claude/hooks/guard-wait-loops.php` returning 500, which is how anybody learned
# `/engcalcs/.claude/settings.json` was served as a plain 200 -- the agent definitions, the hook
# scripts and the permission allow-list, readable by anyone who guessed the path.
#
# **THE FIX MADE THE ALARM WORSE, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF THIS FILE.** Once blocked, those paths
# answer 403, which check.sh also counts as a failure -- so a working fix would have mailed a
# failure every morning for ever. The walk now skips dot-directories as a class, which silences the
# nag AND silences the finding: the watch could no longer see that class of exposure at all, whether
# or not anybody had deployed the fix. A guard that goes quiet when the thing it guards is still
# broken is worse than no guard.
#
# So this file asks the opposite question. A PASS here is 401, 403 or 404. A 200 is a FAILURE and
# names the URL. It is deliberately a SHORT, TYPED list rather than a derived one: the derived-list
# argument that governs the rest of check.sh does not apply, because there is no rule a machine can
# read that says which URLs ought to be unreachable -- that is a judgement, and a judgement belongs
# in a declaration with its reason beside it.
#
# It also closes the deploy gap by construction. An .htaccess does nothing until the file is on the
# server, so this fails from the moment the fix is written until the moment somebody pulls -- which
# is the one thing nothing else here could tell you.

# The Claude Code working directory: agent definitions, hook scripts, and settings.json carrying
# the permission allow-list. Blocked by .claude/.htaccess and by a blanket dot-directory rule in
# the suite's root .htaccess, at two Apache override levels deliberately.
https://hawsedc.com/engcalcs/.claude/settings.json

# The development tree: roadmap, scripts, harnesses, agent journals, translation payloads.
# Blocked by dev/.htaccess since long before this file existed.
https://hawsedc.com/engcalcs/dev/ROADMAP.md

# Usage logs. No row names anybody, but they are personal-adjacent by aggregation.
https://hawsedc.com/engcalcs/log/engcalcs-lang.log

# Editor and CI configuration. Not secret, not a page, and nobody has ever intended to serve them.
https://hawsedc.com/engcalcs/.vscode/settings.json
https://hawsedc.com/engcalcs/.github/copilot-instructions.md

# The git directory. Blocked by a RedirectMatch in the suite's root .htaccess since 2026-07-28,
# when it was found serving a browsable index and handing out intact packfiles.
https://hawsedc.com/engcalcs/.git/config
